02:52:00.732 --> 02:52:01.952
DM: You don't know how you got there.

02:52:02.312 --> 02:52:02.852
Unknown: Yeah.

02:52:02.852 --> 02:52:04.692
DM: And like you're forced to

02:52:05.752 --> 02:52:06.792
DM: interact with each other.

02:52:06.792 --> 02:52:16.932
Delwath: So my favorite crazy hook of games I've ran, this wasn't in Talgar, um, but a while ago I ran a game that started with the PCs being

02:52:16.932 --> 02:52:20.432
Delwath: summoned by a high level wizard to go on a quest.

02:52:21.072 --> 02:52:23.972
Delwath: So like they were just teleported to the, like the first adventure.

02:52:24.012 --> 02:52:25.452
DM: Yeah, that's like the...

02:52:25.452 --> 02:52:28.712
DM: So Schwartz was the only one who pl- played in the Rizvan one-shot.

02:52:29.072 --> 02:52:31.432
DM: And it was like that was the Rizvan one shot with the,

02:52:32.232 --> 02:52:34.452
DM: the dwarven gods summoned everybody-

02:52:34.472 --> 02:52:34.492
Unknown: Yeah

02:52:34.492 --> 02:52:35.892
DM: ... to come help Rizvan.

02:52:35.952 --> 02:52:37.072
Unknown: Yeah. Yeah. No, that-

02:52:37.072 --> 02:52:37.812
DM: That one was fun

02:52:37.812 --> 02:52:41.232
DM: ... I, I mean, starting a long campaign where they really have no idea-

02:52:41.252 --> 02:52:47.872
DM: So I had this idea, like the beginning of the campaign is you're in the brig of a ship.

02:52:48.152 --> 02:52:48.352
Unknown: Right.

02:52:48.632 --> 02:52:49.032
Unknown: You don't know how you got there.

02:52:49.032 --> 02:52:49.972
DM: And you wake up-

02:52:50.492 --> 02:52:50.752
Unknown: That's great

02:52:50.752 --> 02:52:51.992
DM: ... to the sound of the waves-

02:52:52.552 --> 02:52:52.732
Unknown: That's great

02:52:52.732 --> 02:52:53.732
DM: ... rocking back and forth.

02:52:54.052 --> 02:52:54.272
Unknown: Right.

02:52:55.352 --> 02:52:56.932
DM: And that's the like opening scene.

02:52:56.972 --> 02:52:58.812
Kenzo: That's great. I love shit like that.

02:52:58.812 --> 02:53:00.172
Kenzo: It's like really fun, 'cause then you're just like-

02:53:00.192 --> 02:53:00.232
DM: Yeah

02:53:00.232 --> 02:53:01.092
Kenzo: ... "What the fuck is this?"

02:53:01.192 --> 02:53:01.312
DM: Yeah.

02:53:01.332 --> 02:53:02.852
Kenzo: Like it's like a... Like that, that's like a,

02:53:04.412 --> 02:53:06.892
Kenzo: you know, deep into plot twist stuff where you're just like, uh-

02:53:06.972 --> 02:53:07.072
DM: Right.

02:53:07.072 --> 02:53:07.072
Unknown: Wow

02:53:07.072 --> 02:53:09.652
Kenzo: ... this is very surprising and interesting to like learn what the hell's going on.

02:53:09.732 --> 02:53:09.892
Unknown: One,

02:53:10.652 --> 02:53:17.852
Seeker: one of my ideas for the space opera RPG was just inspired by, it's called something like a johatsu scam.

02:53:18.352 --> 02:53:25.492
Seeker: It's something that has happened in Japan where there are these services that help you disappear basically.

02:53:25.732 --> 02:53:26.172
Unknown: Mm.

02:53:26.192 --> 02:53:26.232
DM: Ooh.

02:53:26.232 --> 02:53:29.472
Seeker: Where you're like, "I want to leave my life."

02:53:29.552 --> 02:53:29.572
Unknown: Mm.

02:53:29.572 --> 02:53:30.572
Unknown: Like it's not viable for me-

02:53:30.652 --> 02:53:31.012
Unknown: Yeah

02:53:31.012 --> 02:53:33.552
Seeker: ... to quit my job and get a divorce or whatever.

02:53:33.552 --> 02:53:36.312
Seeker: I'll just pay you some money and you'll relocate me with a new identity.

02:53:36.792 --> 02:53:39.072
Seeker: But some of those services unfortunately

02:53:39.952 --> 02:53:40.792
Unknown: are fraudulent.

02:53:40.992 --> 02:53:42.832
Kenzo: Yeah, of course. Yeah.

02:53:42.832 --> 02:53:44.612
Seeker: And so there are people who

02:53:44.612 --> 02:53:44.832
DM: [laughs]

02:53:44.832 --> 02:53:48.392
Seeker: ... you give them money to disappear and then they're like...

02:53:48.392 --> 02:53:52.452
Seeker: Anyway, so you could make up your own backstory about why you needed to like leave your life.

02:53:52.452 --> 02:53:53.632
Kenzo: That's cool. I love that.

02:53:53.652 --> 02:53:56.792
Seeker: But now you're thrown into this situation where you're trapped somehow.

02:53:57.692 --> 02:53:59.812
